      \field{abstract}{This file contains some Fortran 90 programs to compute associate incomplete elliptic integrals of first and second kind: B(phi|m) and D(phi|m): 1) xelbd.f90: test driver of "elbd" and "relbd" 2) elbd.f90: subroutine to compute B(phi|m) and D(phi|m) in double precision 3) relbd.f90: subroutine to compute B(phi|m) and D(phi|m) in single precision 4) celbd.f90: subroutine to compute B(m) and D(m) in double precision 5) rcelbd.f90:subroutine to compute B(m) and D(m) in single precision Once B(phi|m) and D(phi|m) are given, F(phi|m) and E(phi|m) are computed as F(phi|m) = B(phi|m) + D(phi|m), E(phi|m) = B(phi|m) + (1-m) D(phi|m) Similarly K(m) = B(m) + D(m), E(m) = B(m) + (1-m) D(m) The file also includes the output file of "xelbd"}
